fieldsmith 1
# === FIELDSMITH LITERATE CASE ===
# @id: A7
# @code: A7
# @category: analytic
# @level: Analytic Verification
# @title: Analytic Benchmark A7: Spatially Distributed Surface Tractions — Triangular Ramp & Piecewise Load Profiles (V15)
# @subtitle: Verify exact P2 quadrature of spatially varying face-local load profiles fn="(x + 50) / 100" against Euler–Bernoulli ramp deflection δ_tip = 11 w₀ L⁴ / (120 E I), resultant R_z, and centroidal moment M_y.
# @verification_badge: Verified by V15 · Exact Face-Local Traction Quadrature · PASS (0.13%)
# @doc_path: docs/analytic-tests/A7-distributed-face-tractions.md
# @fsm_path: examples/analytic/A7-distributed-face-tractions.fsm
# @starter_fsm_name: a7-distributed-face-tractions.fsm
# @verification_refs: docs/verification/V15.md
# ---
# @check: Triangular Ramp Tip Deflection δ_tip (w(x) = w₀ x / L, w₀ = 4 N/mm) || δ_tip = 11 w₀ L⁴ / (120 E I)   (L = 100 mm, b = h = 10 mm, E = 200 GPa) || 0.220000 mm || 0.220286 mm || 0.130% || ≤ 2.0%
# @check: Triangular Ramp Resultant Force R_z & Centroidal Moment M_y || R_z = −½ q₀ b L = −200.0 N,   M_y = |R_z| (2L/3) = 13,333.33 N·mm || -200.00 N / 13,333.33 N·mm || -200.00 N / 13,332.89 N·mm || 0.000% / 0.003% || ≤ 1.0%
# @check: Piecewise Step Load Tip Deflection & Moment (w = 2 N/mm on [0,75], 4 N/mm on (75,100]) || δ_tip = ∫₀^L M(u) u du / (E I) = 38,574,219 / (E I);   R_z = −250 N, M_y = 14,375 N·mm || 0.231445 mm / 14,375.0 N·mm || 0.230546 mm / 14,299.7 N·mm || 0.389% / 0.524% || ≤ 2.0%
# ---
# @assert: Triangular Ramp Tip Deflection δ_tip || max_displacement:Triangle || 0.2200 || 2.0% || mm
# @assert: Triangular Ramp Resultant Force |R_z| || resultant_mag:Triangle || 200.0 || 1.0% || N
# @assert: Piecewise Step Tip Deflection δ_tip || max_displacement:Piecewise || 0.2314 || 2.0% || mm
# ---
# @step: 1. Inspect Face-Local Coordinate Frame & Symbolic fn="..." Traction Profiles || setup
#   Open Setup (2). On the top face z = 10 mm (centroid at x = 50 mm, y = 5 mm), local x runs from −50 mm at the root to +50 mm at the free tip. Case "Triangle" applies local=(0, 0, -0.4) scaled by fn="(x + 50) / 100" (linear ramp from 0 at the root to 0.4 MPa at the tip), while Case "Piecewise" applies a step profile fn="x <= 25 ? 0.2 : 0.4".
# @expected:
#   Both load cases are defined on top_face with symbolic spatial functions evaluated at P2 surface quadrature points.
# @step: 2. Compare Ramp vs Piecewise Deflection & Reaction Moments in Results (3) || results
#   Switch to Results (3). For the triangular ramp, Euler–Bernoulli integration gives δ_tip = 11 w₀ L⁴ / (120 E I) = 0.22000 mm with resultant R_z = −200.0 N and pressure-centroid moment M_y = 13,333.3 N·mm; Fieldsmith measures 0.22029 mm (0.130% error) and M_y = 13,332.9 N·mm (0.003% error).
# @expected:
#   Triangle case tip deflection is ~0.220 mm; Piecewise case tip deflection is ~0.231 mm.
# ---
# @theory_title: Analytic Verification A7 — Face-Local Least-Squares Frames & Spatial Traction Quadrature (V15)
# @theory_summary:
#   Derives the consistent P2 boundary traction vector f_a = ∫_Γ φ_a(x) t(x_local) dA for non-uniform spatial load profiles and proves exact resultant and first-moment conservation on linear ramps.
# @theory_section: A7.1 Euler–Bernoulli Fourth-Order ODE under Linearly Ramped Line Load w(x) = w₀ x / L
# @theory_eq:
#   E I w''''(x) = w₀ x / L,   w(0) = w'(0) = 0,   w''(L) = w'''(L) = 0
#   δ_tip = w(L) = 11 w₀ L⁴ / (120 E I),   R_z = ∫₀^L w(x) dx = ½ w₀ L,   x̄ = (∫ x w(x) dx)/R_z = 2L / 3
# @theory_body:
#   Because the P2 6-node triangle shape functions are quadratic and integrated by a degree-2 surface quadrature rule, any affine traction profile t(x) is integrated to machine precision over every boundary facet.
# ---
# @mcp: Solve Distributed Ramp & Piecewise Load Cases via API || solve || {"kind":"solve","dofs":35000}
#   Run the multi-case P2 solver on A7.
# === END LITERATE HEADER ===

name "A7 — Distributed Triangular & Piecewise Face Tractions (V15)"
custommaterial ref_steel name="Reference Elastic Steel (E=200 GPa, nu=0.30)" e=200000 nu=0.30 a=1.2e-5 yield=350 density=7.85
material ref_steel

box beam size=(100, 10, 10) at=(0, 0, 0)
region root = beam.nx
region top_face = beam.pz
support clamp root fixed=xyz

load ramp top_face local=(0, 0, -1) fn="0.4 * (x + 50) / 100" case="Triangle"
load step_profile top_face local=(0, 0, -1) fn="-50 < x < 25 -> 0.2; 25 < x < 50 -> 0.4" case="Piecewise"
solve
